    "created_at": "2016-05-25T16:19:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-25T16:19:40Z",
    "body": "The magic is that an empty string for SetHash is converted into `#`, which then is stored in the URL as a hash of length zero. The fact that it exists (regardless of length) is enough to trigger the short-circuit load code in nsDocShell::LoadURI, which calls `currentURI->EqualsExceptRef(aURI, &sameExceptHashes)` and succeeds.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
