    "created_at": "2016-05-25T16:54:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-25T16:54:53Z",
    "body": "So browsers have an additional state for \"missing\" fragment which only surfaces here? That is, we have `https://example.com/` where fragment is null, `https://example.com/#` where fragment is the empty string, and this new `https://example.com/`.hash = \"\", where fragment is null, but \"hasFragment\" is true. And hasFragment is only relevant for navigation?\n\n@valenting, thoughts?\n\nIf that really only is a thing for navigation, I'd say we make `location.hash` pass an additional flag to the navigate algorithm rather than complicating all URLs.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
