    "created_at": "2016-05-25T17:04:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-25T17:04:05Z",
    "body": "```\n7:01 PM <bz> So in Chrome...\n7:01 PM <bz> I start at http://foo.com/ in URL bar\n7:01 PM <bz> I set location.hash = \"\", URL bar shows \"http://foo.com/\"\n7:01 PM <bz> I set location.hash = \"bar\", URL bar shows \"http://foo.com/#bar\"\n7:01 PM <bz> I set location.hash = \"\", URL bar shows \"http://foo.com/#\"\n7:02 PM <bz> I _think_ the web compat constraint is that if you're at \"http://foo.com/#bar\" and you set location.hash = \"\" there should be no actual navigation\n```\n\nAnd in Gecko apparently it always goes to `#`, which is different from how it behaves for `new URL()`, but seems better than the rather weird behavior Chrome has.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
